[
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fintype.card_ofFinset#doc\">docs#Fintype.card_ofFinset</a> doesn't seem to like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.fintypeUIcc#doc\">docs#Set.fintypeUIcc</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocallyFiniteOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: unsolved goals -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works with `respectTransparency.types`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backward</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respectTransparency</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">types</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works with `apply`/`exact`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- works with `Icc` instead of `uIcc`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Icc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- this is probably the cause, but `Set.fintypeUIcc` is an `instance`</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- so it's `@[instance_reducible]`, so this should work</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: Tactic `rfl` failed -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">substring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fintypeUIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">with_implicit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 620546740,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788244434
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fintype.card_ofFinset#doc\">docs#Fintype.card_ofFinset</a> has a hardcoded <code>Fintype</code> instance in its type:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.fintypeUIcc#doc\">docs#Set.fintypeUIcc</a> is defined using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fintype.ofFinset#doc\">docs#Fintype.ofFinset</a>, so <code>H</code> should be picked up from the instance.<br>\n<a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.instFintypeIcc#doc\">docs#Set.instFintypeIcc</a> is defined the same way and it does work (although <code>with_implicit rfl</code> fails for it too).</p>\n<p>This isn't the first time <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Fintype.card_ofFinset#doc\">docs#Fintype.card_ofFinset</a> is being annoying, but usually it's because of the hardcoded <code>Fintype</code> instance in it, and this time it should work in my favor! What am I missing? Why isn't the <code>with_implicit rfl</code> working? Why does it work for <code>Icc</code>?</p>",
        "id": 620546875,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788244469
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_coe</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">coe_uIcc</span><span class=\"o\">])]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>this works</p>",
        "id": 620586382,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1788253467
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Transparency.20problems.20with.20Fintype.20and.20Set.2EuIcc/near/620546740\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- works with `apply`/`exact`</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Note that <code>with_implicit apply/exact</code> fails, so this is just hiding the defEq abuse</p>",
        "id": 620586774,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1788253552
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes that's what the question is about</p>",
        "id": 620587730,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788253740
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The proof doesn't have the right type:<br>\nIn the declaration <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Set.fintypeUIcc#doc\">docs#Set.fintypeUIcc</a>, the type of the completeness proof is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which doesn't unify with the required type</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>under implicit reducibility</p>",
        "id": 620591661,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788254561
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I thought proofs were in the private scope?</p>",
        "id": 620607607,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1788257993
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, if you used <code>by</code> then yes. But even then, we still have a proof term that could have the wrong type</p>",
        "id": 620608336,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788258165
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fintypeUIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_uIcc</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>seems to fix it</p>",
        "id": 620609017,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788258351
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Huh, that's strange; could we detect this wrong type issue at the <code>instance</code> with some linter?<br>\nHow come <code>rw</code> manages to find a term to rewrite with <code>Fintype.card_ofFinset</code> but doesn't solve the side condition? I would imagine it does a defeq check with <code>@Fintype.card ?p (ofFinset ?s ?H)</code> on the goal and would only succeed if the unification succeeds. So where does <code>H</code> go missing in the process?</p>",
        "id": 620614013,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788259620
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Proof unification can happen with proof irrelevance</p>",
        "id": 620614155,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788259649
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So since the types don't match (under implicit transparency), the metavariable stays unassigned</p>",
        "id": 620614203,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788259662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So why doesn't <code>rw</code> fail with the usual <code>Did not find an occurrence of the pattern</code>?</p>",
        "id": 620614736,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788259789
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It did find an occurrence of the pattern; the types not matching doesn't mean defeq fails but that it just doesn't assign the metavariable, since we have proof irrelevance</p>",
        "id": 620615093,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788259873
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually no that's not quite right; it found a different way to solve the unification problem by unfolding the instance</p>",
        "id": 620617266,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788260422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One that doesn't reach <code>?H</code> though</p>",
        "id": 620617397,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788260456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Because <code>?H</code> gets eliminated in the unfolding process</p>",
        "id": 620617519,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788260484
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So how does <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false</code> fix it? Wouldn't it still do the same (if not more) unfolding, eliminating <code>H</code>?</p>",
        "id": 620620693,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788261304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Great analysis, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"873547\">@Robin Arnez</span>!</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Transparency.20problems.20with.20Fintype.20and.20Set.2EuIcc/near/620620693\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So how does <code>set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false</code> fix it? Wouldn't it still do the same (if not more) unfolding, eliminating <code>H</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Here is the relevant trace excerpt, pre-filtered if you want to expect it in Live Lean:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"n\">meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PostprocessTraces</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PostprocessTraces</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Lattice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LocallyFiniteOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">[Meta.isDefEq] ✅️ Fintype.card ↑(Set.uIcc a b) =?= Fintype.card ↑?m.12 ▼</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  [] ✅️ Set.fintypeUIcc a b =?= Fintype.ofFinset ?s ?H ▼</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    [] ✅️ Fintype.ofFinset (Finset.uIcc a b) ⋯ =?= Fintype.ofFinset ?s ?H ▼</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      [] ✅️ Finset.uIcc a b =?= ?s ▶</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      [] ❌️ fun x =&gt; Finset.mem_uIcc =?= ?H ▶</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      [] ✅️ Fintype.subtype (Finset.uIcc a b) ⋯ =?= Fintype.subtype ?s ?H ▶</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"n\">postprocess_traces</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">filterSubtrees</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">containsString</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Fintype.ofFinset (Finset.uIcc a b)\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exposeSubtrees</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">containsString</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Fintype.subtype\"</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Meta</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card_ofFinset</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Lean ends up in a comparison of <code>Fintype.finset</code> applications. First, it tries to match them structurally, by congruence, before further reducing the heads to <code>Fintype.subtype</code>. This is where <code>?H</code> should have been assigned. Because of the defeq problems, <code>?H</code> cannot be assigned, so the congruence pass fails. Only then does Lean further reduce the heads.</p>\n<p>So even if the transparency is increased, Lean first tries to close the defeq problem by congruence. This is often faster and is usually what users expect: Also in this case, it would be a better experience if <code>?H</code> was being assigned instead of doing more unfolding.</p>",
        "id": 620630077,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1788263370
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah and <code>backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types</code> causes the unification to succeed because it unifies them under default transparency, right?</p>",
        "id": 620630456,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1788263449
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Transparency.20problems.20with.20Fintype.20and.20Set.2EuIcc/near/620607607\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I thought proofs were in the private scope?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I don't like this behavior either (and also encountered problems like this before).</p>\n<p>I considered whether the elaborator could automatically insert <code>id</code> in some places, so that we'd effectively get</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fintypeUIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ofFinset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">uIcc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_uIcc</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which should work, too (because it hides the proof term with the \"wrong\" type inside of a proof term that has the expected type). However, This causes a different kind of problem: In some cases we then get <code>id ?m =?= x</code> instead of <code>?m =?= x</code>, preventing  <code>?m</code> from being assigned.</p>",
        "id": 620633540,
        "sender_full_name": "Paul Reichert",
        "timestamp": 1788264073
    }
]